This wasn't a particularly major one in my mind, but there are some
fairly invasive changes, so I went ahead and broke save and stuck a
couple smaller things in alongside.

The "autowield your default launcher" was obviously discussed here for a
bit, and now it's going to get to see play; hopefully, the "lava spill"
stuff adds to the atmosphere as much as I hope it will.  The Windows
binaries will probably be updated tomorrow night.

Changes since last week...

10/14:
* 'F'iring arrows will now autowield your default launcher first, if you 
  have one selected
-- Corresponding new command: %, allows you to ready a default launcher.
-- (yes, it's unintuitive, but it's also one of the only non-extended 
    command keys left)
* Iron safes: Cannot be kicked or forced: extremely low chance to crack 
  unless you're a Rogue
-- Magical opening methods work fine; you'll need a stethoscope for manually
-- Only show up deeper in the dungeon, but may have more treasure inside
-- Known interface issue: if you're cracking it while standing on it, you 
   must use > instead of . due to existing stethoscope functionality
* Falling rocks trap (sic): only appears beyond level 15
* Gehennom may have lava spills into the room areas... watch your step!
* Token humor: New type of bag that's a longer-lasting light source... at 
  the cost of stealth.
* Bug fix: One shopkeeper wand message was mis-displaying
* Bug fix: Demon princes won't generate weird money2mon errors if you aren't 
  carrying gold when they ask for a bribe
* Bug tracker: The mysterious monsndx panic() bug will now try to report what 
  monster it was thinking of when it freaked.  This has only happened
  twice recently, so this is not a very common bug, which makes it all
  the more easy to find </sarcasm>
* Version updated: 0.4.1

10/10:
* Messages related to monsters teleporting you cleaned up
* Thrown/fired stuff now all gets a reduced strength bonus.
-- This is a tiny increase for 'fired' stuff, and a big decrease for 
   'just hucked'.
-- This also fixes the bug with wielding a two-hander and GoP and getting 
   +14 to thrown darts.  Oops.
* Speculative fix related to stuff stepping on stuff even if it can't see you

10/9:
* Speculative bug fix related to summon-nasties code


